    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Great to have you along for the ride. Thanks a lot for stopping by. I'm really glad I haven't been back. Of course, the House Oversight Committee chair, it's James Comer, district one represented at the great state of Kentucky. James, how are you? Good to see you again. Thanks for having me on big news day. You know, it was interesting. I had Ellen Dershowitz on yesterday. We talked a lot about how ridiculous this case is. He's 86 now. He said in his 60 years plus practicing law, he's never seen a worse criminal case ever. This is the worst case he's ever seen at a New York City. This judge were shunned case. This 34 felonies made out of expired misdemeanors. He's never seen anything like it. But he did think that we're Sean would try to sentence Trump. We just found out today, obviously little while ago that we're Sean has now put it off until after the election. I'm hearing the Democrats might have pressured him to do that because convicting him or sentencing I should say would actually hurt Kamala Harris. What are your thoughts about the big news today at New York?",
