  {
    "episode_id": 91319,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91319.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's a great question. We've got Jim Jordan and I talked about that. Obviously, he's chairman of the judiciary committee. We have a weaponization select committee. It looks like the main thing that the committees can do is expose the truth, expose the corruption, give the American people the truth. What we can do that unfortunately the Republicans have proven unwilling to do is cut the budget, exercise the power of the purse. We're supposed to have a system of checks and balances to where if you have a bad member of the judiciary, there's someone in the Department of Justice or there's someone in the judiciary branch or the executive branch that can step in and hold them accountable. But what's happening now is they're all on the same team. You've got all the corrupt judiciary with one ideology and that is obviously a very left-wing ideology and they all have one goal and that's to take down Donald Trump. So the whole system of checks and balances has been thrown out the window. The one thing Congress could do legislatively is cut budgets but at the end of the day you know it doesn't appear that's going to happen but we will continue to give the American people the truth and try to bring these people in and expose them for what they are their complete frauds.",
