    "turn_text": "saying this for two years. I'm the one guy that would go on conservative shows and say, we do not need a special counsel. And there would be some of the far right members of Congress that would come up. We need a special counsel, we need a special counsel. The reason I don't like special counsels is what we're talking about now. Congress really doesn't have any authority to do anything to stop them. They're created to be independent of everything. Even with everything that arises, even with the recent assassination attempt on Trump, I still saw conservatives run on the podcast and conservative media say, we need a special counsel and I want to pull my hair out. Because the whole special counsel process is based on the assumption that you trust the Attorney General to appoint someone fair. And we do not. Merrick Garland is attorney general. He's not going to appoint anyone fair. I have zero confidence in Merrick Garland. But even if we have a Republican attorney general, that's a good attorney general. I still think we need to do away with the special counsel because there's no accountability. They're not required to be transparent. They're on no timeline. And they have an endless supply of money in their budget. So I just think that the whole special counsel business model needs to be done away with.",
